    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 7th with a high-upside offensive slate, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who represents our premier play today. While his #8 spot in the order is suboptimal, his matchup against Lowder (4.77 xERA) and the significant wind-out benefit maximize his stolen base potential, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 Roto landscape. **Junior Caminero** (71.24) follows closely; despite the lineup being technically pending, his spot at the heart of the order against a left-handed arm provides the best blend of contact profile and volume, justifying his high score despite the traditional platoon disadvantage.\n\n**Trea Turner** (67.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.86) remain bankable anchors against Ginn. While Ginn is a decent mid-rotation arm, the slow delivery speed is a massive tactical advantage for **Trea Turner**, whose elite burst adds meaningful points to his projected efficiency. **Caleb Durbin** (42.95) remains the toughest decision of the day. While his raw base projection is middling, the specific combination of his high-percentile stolen base upside and the slow delivery of Jax forces him into a starting role despite his #9 spot in the lineup. Our bench remains stagnant today due to the absence of active games for stars like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**, while **Christian Yelich** remains sidelined on the IL. We are monitoring the status of **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, and **Lars Nootbaar** closely to see if they might provide a late-week infusion of speed to support our core group of **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena**.",
